  "question": {
    "text": "Let $[x]$ denote the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$. Then the domain of $f(x)=\\sec ^{-1}(2[x]+1)$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KdWYB",
      "text": "$(-\\infty,-1] \\cup[0, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DGrCA",
      "text": "$(-\\infty,-1] \\cup[1, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FDkWj",
      "text": "$(-\\infty, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ro93r",
      "text": "$(-\\infty, \\infty)-\\{0\\}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{ll}\nf(x)=\\sec ^{-1}(2[x]+1) \\\\\n\\Rightarrow 2[x]+1 \\geq 1 & \\text { or } 2[x]+1 \\leq-1 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow 2[x] \\geq 0 & \\text { or } 2[x] \\leq-2 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow[x] \\geq 0 & \\text { or }[x] \\leq-1 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow x \\geq 0 & \\text { or } x \\leq 0\n\\end{array}$\nDomain of $f(x)$ is $(-\\infty, \\infty)$",
    "image": null
  },
